WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.350
- [Narrator] This is the A100
chip from the US giant NVIDIA.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.620
It's one of the world's most
advanced computing processors,

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.080
which helps develop artificial
intelligence that's used

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.120
in everything from self-driving cars

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.120
to making drugs and even building weapons.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.490
And this is one of its
newest competitors made

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.780
by a Chinese startup.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.490
Industry analysts who track the speed

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.240
of chips say this model is
even faster than the A100

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.920
based on initial tests.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.717
- It produced performances
that were significantly

00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:33.540
more competitive than previous
AI chips coming from China.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.280
- [Narrator] Here's how
the design and capabilities

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.840
of these two chips compare

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.783
as the race for dominance
in tech is ramping up.

00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:42.360
(pensive music)

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.740
The US has been a pioneer

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.950
in the semiconductor
industry for over 70 years.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.780
- The US essentially gave birth

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.130
to the semiconductor industry
and the semiconductor economy.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.990
- Wayne Lam is the director of research

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.930
with tech consulting firm CCS Insight.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.010
For over a decade,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.680
he has been researching
American chip technology.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.810
- [Wayne] The US was an ideal place

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:08.220
because it started much at the
research and core sciences.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.570
- [Narrator] In the late 1940s,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.600
American scientists invented
the first transistor,

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.810
the fundamental technology
behind all chips.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.330
Early versions of chips
fit inside computers

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.010
that helped calculate projectiles

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.154
and get NASA space
programs off the ground.

00:01:23.154 --> 00:01:24.810
(lively music)

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.310
But the industry really took off

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.590
in the 1960s with the rising demand

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.043
for consumer goods like televisions
and corporate computers.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.040
That boom also drove chip companies

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.870
to spring up across Asia

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.690
with Taiwan Semiconductor
Manufacturing Company

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.730
now leading the industry, making more

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.660
than 90% of the world's
most advanced chips.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.370
Still today, the US is home

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.530
to some of the world's
leading chip designers

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.000
and they help power everything

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.630
from our smartphones to
laptops and data centers.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.570
China, on the other hand,
has long been trailing the US

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.670
and for several decades
it has actually relied

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.080
on American companies,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.140
as well as chip makers
in Taiwan and Japan.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.180
In 2021, China imported more

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:11.180
than $430 billion worth of
chips, exceeding that of oil.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.260
So Chinese President Xi Jinping

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.990
has made it a top priority to change that.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:19.380
- It's absolutely important
on a strategic basis.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.060
- Gregory Allen is a senior fellow

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.000
at the Center for Strategic
and International Studies,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.490
a think tank based in Washington, D.C.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.320
He's been following Beijing's AI

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.860
and semiconductor policies
for about seven years.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.150
- [Gregory] What they essentially wanted

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.460
in the semiconductor industry was for more

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.540
of the chips that were used
in China to be made in China.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.220
- [Narrator] So to
become more self-reliant,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.550
Beijing promised to
provide about $180 billion

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.613
in state funding to support
its domestic chip industry.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.090
The goal is to design
chips that can be as fast

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.360
as the American ones like
this AI chip from NVIDIA.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.040
And this model released in August

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.450
by Biren is the latest
demonstration of China's progress.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.740
Like its American rival,

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.590
the Biren chip is also a
graphics processing unit,

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.930
or GPU, and both are designed

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.873
to help computers perform
complex tasks faster.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.260
So what makes a chip powerful?

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.460
To improve their performance,

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.210
both companies are using
the same type of transistor.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.940
It's the fundamental unit that
basically controls the flow

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.380
of electronic signals

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:26.430
and that allows the chips to
store data or run calculations.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.490
But unlike the first transistor
invented in the 1940s,

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.260
the ones today are so small

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.150
that they are measured in nanometers,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.030
which is a fraction of
the width of a human hair.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.370
Seven nanometer transistors
are now the base

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.370
for both NVIDIA and Biren's high-end chips

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.440
- So smaller to the transistor,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.300
the more transistors you can pack

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.660
into the same surface area of a silicon.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.070
- [Narrator] The American chip is designed

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:52.470
with more than 54 billion transistors

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.500
over a plate of about
800 millimeters square

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.660
whereas the BR100 is slightly bigger

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.060
with about 77 billion transistors packed

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.332
into about 1,000 square millimeters.

00:04:03.332 --> 00:04:04.770
While there are many
factors that determine

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.880
a chip's performance,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.790
industry experts say having a
higher number of transistors

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.000
can help increase the
Chinese processor's speed.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.920
Biren says its chip can perform more

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.730
than 1,000 trillion operations
per second at its peak.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.640
Write it out, that's 15 zeros.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.213
That's about three times the
stated speed of NVIDIA's A100.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.900
But whether Biren will be
able to dominate the market

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.330
will require more than designing chips.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.060
Producing them is also a huge challenge

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.190
because it requires precise manufacturing

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.440
to squeeze these billions of transistors

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.880
onto a tiny surface.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.670
- Semiconductor manufacturing is perhaps

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.070
the most technologically complicated thing

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.650
that the human species does.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.450
- [Narrator] One of the
most complex processes

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.800
is called lithography,

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.410
which blasts UV light through photo masks

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.690
and prints patterns on silicon wafers,

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.300
adding layers to form the transistors.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.400
- You need to be precise.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.540
Some of the layers

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:05.220
in the semiconductor transistors
are only one atom thick.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.840
- [Narrator] So NVIDIA and Biren both look

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.880
to another company for manufacturing.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:09.870
You may have guessed,

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.540
that's the Taiwan Semiconductor
Manufacturing Company,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.943
the world's largest
contract chip producer.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.080
But Biren's reliance on TSMC

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.900
is becoming a hurdle on
its way to rivaling NVIDIA.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.970
- Has been sort of a cautionary tale

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.643
for the Chinese semiconductor industry.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.523
- [Narrator] A couple of months

00:05:28.523 --> 00:05:30.360
after the Chinese
startup release its chip,

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.990
the Biden administration
imposed new export restrictions.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:36.270
The rules barred cutting-edge
semiconductors made

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.750
with American technologies
from being sold to China.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.330
And because TSMC uses
equipment from US companies,

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.400
Biren is at risk

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.400
of losing the Taiwanese
chip maker as a supplier.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.490
- This dramatically
reduces Biren's prospects

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.760
for its future as a leading chip designer.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.760
- [Narrator] Biren didn't
respond to a request for comment.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:00.150
TSMC says it complies with
all laws and regulations

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.763
but declined to comment
on specific customers.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.820
China also depends on a handful

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.980
of American companies
that dominate the industry

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.380
for advanced manufacturing equipment.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.120
With the American
government blocking China

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.760
from buying these machines,
it becomes even harder

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.093
for Beijing to build its own
high-end chip making factories.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.100
- That development is a Herculean
effort to say the least.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.880
So it would require
considerable investment

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.820
in capital and time to make that happen.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:30.990
- [Narrator] China isn't alone

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.310
in facing challenges in trying

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.410
to become more self-sufficient.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.540
While the US leads in design and research,

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.120
it has also long relied
on outside manufacturers

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.570
like TSMC and Samsung in South Korea.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:45.060
And the vulnerability of that
dependence became an issue

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:48.120
during the pandemic when a chip
shortage hit companies large

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.700
and small, prompting
President Biden to promise

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.520
that more semiconductors
would be produced in the US.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.770
- This is infrastructure.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.530
So look, we need to
build the infrastructure

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:01.863
of today, not repair the one of yesterday.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.070
- [Narrator] So in August,
he signed the CHIPS Act,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.410
allocating more than $52 billion

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:11.220
in federal aid for semiconductor
research and manufacturing.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.640
TSMC later announced that
it would invest $40 billion

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.070
to build two factories in Arizona.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:19.050
- These investments are helping us build

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:22.500
and strengthen the supply
chain here in America.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.970
- [Narrator] And only
months after the release

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.610
of China's BR100, NVIDIA announced

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.040
that it will release
a super fast new chip,

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.710
which would in turn beat Biren's.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.300
The long and expensive race

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.070
to develop chips that'll drive the future

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.489
of AI is entering a new phase.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:40.156
(pensive music)

